<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6583] Methods of rebalancing progress metrics must obey JavaBean naming conventions</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6583</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Notes&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Notes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Getters for &lt;b&gt;rebalancingStartTime&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;estimateRebalancingFinishTime&lt;/b&gt; metrics from &lt;b&gt;CacheMetrics&lt;/b&gt; interface don&apos;t follow JavaBean naming conventions; method names don&apos;t start with &lt;b&gt;get&lt;/b&gt; prefix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a result metrics cannot be accessed via MXBean interface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;AcceptanceCriteria&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Acceptance Criteria&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Methods &lt;b&gt;getRebalancingStartTime&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;getEstimateRebalancingFinishTime&lt;/b&gt; are introduced to &lt;b&gt;CacheMetrics&lt;/b&gt; interface.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Existing methods &lt;b&gt;rebalancingStartTime&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;estimateRebalancingFinishTime&lt;/b&gt; are declared as deprecated and will be deleted in future major release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</description>
